# `reporting/posters/` — Conference posters

One folder per poster, named by **date + venue**: `YYYY-MM-venue/`
(e.g. `2026-09-sfn/`). Like talks, a poster is a dated one-off — make a new folder
for a new conference, don't overwrite.

## Format & figures
Large-format single page. Build from the shared `../_assets/lab.cls` (a
poster-size class such as `tikzposter`/`beamerposter`, or `LaTeX`
→ LaTeX) so it matches lab style.

- **Use `../../results/figures/light/`** — posters are printed, so light/print
  figures, and check they hold up at **high DPI and large physical size** (a plot
  that reads fine in a paper can look thin on an A0 board). Set the target size in
  `conf/theme/` if you keep a poster figure variant.
- Reference figures; don't paste-and-forget. Record the results git SHA /
  {{ data_versioning }} rev the poster was built from.

## Keep the printed version
Archive the exact PDF you sent to the printer (poster deadlines are real and the
printed artifact is what people saw) — same freeze logic as paper submissions.
